IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rta-types`
IMPORT `rta-dates`
IMPORT `rta-application`
IMPORT `rta-money`
IMPORT `rta-termination`
IMPORT `rta-entry`
IMPORT `rta-tribunal`
IMPORT `rta-goal`

-- Independent tests for the Residential Tenancies Act 1986 (NZ) encoding.
-- Every expected value comes from independent-expectations.md, written from
-- the Act before the encoding was opened. Scenario ids (A01 ...) refer to
-- that file. A failing assertion is a finding: do not edit expected values.

§ `Independent tests`

-- Calendars: Matariki 2026 and 2027 always supplied; anniversary day only in calWg.
calNZ MEANS `Local calendar` OF (LIST (Date 10 7 2026), (Date 25 6 2027)), EMPTY
calWg MEANS `Local calendar` OF (LIST (Date 10 7 2026), (Date 25 6 2027)), (LIST (Date 25 1 2027))

-- Helpers to build records.
GIVEN wh IS A `Who gives notice`
      kd IS A `Kind of tenancy`
      gr IS A `Ground for notice`
      sd IS A DATE
      mv IS A `Means of service`
      vd IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Termination notice`
tn wh kd gr sd mv vd MEANS `Termination notice` OF wh, kd, gr, sd, mv, vd, TRUE, NOTHING

GIVEN wh IS A `Who gives notice`
      kd IS A `Kind of tenancy`
      gr IS A `Ground for notice`
      sd IS A DATE
      mv IS A `Means of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
earliestT wh kd gr sd mv MEANS `the earliest date to vacate under the notice` (tn wh kd gr sd mv sd) `, calendar` calNZ

GIVEN wd1 IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
isWD wd1 MEANS `is a working day under s 2` wd1 calNZ

GIVEN nn IS A NUMBER, dd IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
nthWD nn dd MEANS `the` nn `th working day after` dd `, calendar` calNZ

-- Tenancy for application tests
GIVEN ex IS AN `Exclusion from the Act`, agr IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Tenancy
ten ex agr MEANS Tenancy OF ex, agr, NOTHING, FALSE, 0

GIVEN ft IS A NUMBER, wr IS A BOOLEAN, tot IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Tenancy
shortTen ft wr tot MEANS Tenancy OF `none of the s 5 exclusions`, FALSE, JUST ft, wr, tot

-- Bond demand helper: kind, amount, weekly rent, keeps pet, agreed, pet bond held, other security
GIVEN kb IS A `Kind of bond`, amt IS A NUMBER, wk IS A NUMBER, kp IS A BOOLEAN, ag IS A BOOLEAN, held IS A BOOLEAN, sec IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
bondOK kb amt wk kp ag held sec MEANS `the landlord may require the bond` (`Bond demand` OF kb, amt, wk, kp, ag, held, sec)

-- Rent increase helper: given, takes effect, written, commenced, last increase, fixed, permits, boarding, order, new rent
GIVEN gv IS A DATE, te IS A DATE, wr IS A BOOLEAN, cm IS A DATE, li IS A MAYBE DATE, fx IS A BOOLEAN, pm IS A BOOLEAN, bh IS A BOOLEAN, mo IS A MAYBE NUMBER, nr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Rent increase notice`
rin gv te wr cm li fx pm bh mo nr MEANS `Rent increase notice` OF gv, te, wr, cm, li, fx, pm, bh, mo, nr

-- Damage helper: s49B(1), careless, cost, insured, irrecoverable, excess, income-related, rent, market rent
GIVEN i1 IS A BOOLEAN, ca IS A BOOLEAN, co IS A NUMBER, ins IS A BOOLEAN, irr IS A BOOLEAN, exs IS A NUMBER, irr2 IS A BOOLEAN, rw IS A NUMBER, mr IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
dmg i1 ca co ins irr exs irr2 rw mr MEANS `the tenant's liability for the damage` (`Damage facts` OF i1, ca, co, ins, irr, exs, irr2, rw, mr)

-- Occasion helper (unpaid, notice same day as occasion)
GIVEN od IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Occasion
occ od MEANS Occasion OF od, NOTHING, od

-- Termination application helper: filed, periodic, arrears, overdue occasions, asb occasions, content ok, damage, assault, remedied, 55A(3)
GIVEN fd IS A DATE
      pr IS A BOOLEAN
      ar IS A NUMBER
      ro IS A LIST OF Occasion
      ao IS A LIST OF Occasion
      ct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Termination application`
tapp fd pr ar ro ao ct MEANS `Termination application` OF fd, pr, ar, ro, ao, ct, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- Fixed term ending helper
GIVEN ex2 IS A DATE, ln IS A NUMBER, rn IS A BOOLEAN, ng IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
contPeriodic ex2 ln rn ng MEANS `the tenancy continues as a periodic tenancy` (`Fixed term ending` OF ex2, ln, rn, FALSE, ng, FALSE)

-- Entry helper: purpose, notice date, notice hour, entry date, entry hour, last inspection, arrears, abandonment belief
GIVEN pu IS A `Purpose of entry`, nd IS A DATE, nh IS A NUMBER, ed IS A DATE, eh IS A NUMBER, li2 IS A MAYBE DATE, ar2 IS A NUMBER, rc IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
entryOK pu nd nh ed eh li2 ar2 rc MEANS `the landlord may enter` (`Entry notice` OF pu, nd, nh, ed, eh, li2, ar2, rc)

GIVEN nd IS A DATE, nh IS A NUMBER, ed IS A DATE, eh IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
roomOK nd nh ed eh MEANS `the landlord may enter the boarding room on notice` (`Boarding room entry` OF nd, nh, ed, eh, TRUE)

-- Boarding house notice helper: ground, given date/hour, effect date/hour, arrears period, arrears paid
GIVEN bg IS A `Boarding house ground`, gd IS A DATE, gh IS A NUMBER, efd IS A DATE, efh IS A NUMBER, ap IS A NUMBER, pd IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
bht bg gd gh efd efh ap pd MEANS `the boarding house termination is lawful` (`Boarding house notice` OF bg, gd, gh, efd, efh, TRUE, ap, pd)

-- Unlawful act application helper: applicant, bond/records flag, committed, terminated, CE aware, made, intentional, retaliatory, just, sought, max
GIVEN apl IS A `Who applies`, fl IS A BOOLEAN, cmt IS A DATE, trm IS A MAYBE DATE, aw IS A MAYBE DATE, mdd IS A DATE, it IS A BOOLEAN, rt IS A BOOLEAN, js IS A BOOLEAN, sg IS A NUMBER, mx IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Unlawful act application`
ua apl fl cmt trm aw mdd it rt js sg mx MEANS `Unlawful act application` OF apl, fl, cmt, trm, aw, mdd, it, rt, js, sg, mx

§§ `Goal 1 — working days and application`

